{{Draftnotes
| name = Chronosphere
| desc = {{H|Faceless Void}} is {{M|innate|text=innately}} immune to the ability's offensive components.
}}

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Chronosphere icon0}}
| desc = Creates a blister in spacetime, trapping all units caught in its sphere of influence and causes you to move very quickly inside it. Only Faceless Void and any units he controls are unaffected. Invisible enemies in the sphere will be revealed.
}}
* Most abilities or items can move units out of Chronosphere, except the following:
** {{A|Batrider|Flaming Lasso}}
** {{A|Bane|Nightmare}} [{{tooltip|?|After end of invulnerability}}]
** {{I|Force Boots}}
** {{I|Force Staff}}-based items.
** {{A|Earth Spirit|Geomagnetic Grip}} [{{tooltip|?|Enchant Remnant can still be pushed in Chronosphere}}]
** {{A|Harpoon|Draw Forth}} [{{tooltip|?|If casted while unit in Chronosphere, goes into cd without doing anything}}]
** {{A|Largo|Catchy Lick}}
** {{A|Marci|Dispose}}
** {{A|Marci|Rebound (Alt-Cast)}}
** {{A|Meepo|MegaMeepo}}
** {{A|Naga Siren|Reel In}}
** {{A|Rubick|Telekinesis}}
** {{A|Snapfire|Firesnap Cookie}}
** {{A|Spirit Bear|Fetch}}
** {{A|Tusk|Snowball}} (Grab Ally)
** {{A|Windranger|Gale Force}}
** {{M|Fear}} sources
** {{M|Taunt}} sources
** Self-{{M|forced movement}} sources.

* {{Symbol|fx|v}}
** {{cf|Cos}} Has a 0.6-{{M|cast backswing}} with {{Cl|Claszian Apostasy|Faceless Void}} equipped.

